title: Maren
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_stones == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Maren: Sergeant Maren, the watch. Such as it is. You are the Countess's map maker? #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0100_Maren
Maren: Then you can do me a service. Somebody moves the boundary stones by the bridge. At night, every night, a pace or two. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0200_Maren
Maren: The hearing is in a week, and the stones walk. Watch them for me, after dark, and tell me who it is. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0300_Maren
-> I will watch them. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0400
    Maren: Good. I need a name, not a story. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0500_Maren
    <<set $quest_stones to QuestState.Active>>
-> Stones are your business, not mine. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0600
    Maren: They are on your map, aren't they? Think about it. #line:Maren.16dbcb8b_0700_Maren
    <<set $quest_stones to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed stones>>
===

title: Maren
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_stones == QuestState.Offered
---
Maren: Changed your mind about the stones? #line:Maren.fec2ae5c_0100_Maren
-> I will watch them tonight. #line:Maren.fec2ae5c_0200
    Maren: Good. #line:Maren.fec2ae5c_0300_Maren
    <<set $quest_stones to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed stones>>
-> No. #line:Maren.fec2ae5c_0400
    Maren: Then don't stand in the light. #line:Maren.fec2ae5c_0500_Maren
===

title: Maren
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_stones == QuestState.Active and not $saw_lio
---
Maren: The stones move after dark. You won't see anything standing here at noon. #line:Maren.1b4b693c_0100_Maren
===

title: Maren
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_stones == QuestState.Active and $saw_lio
---
// The second fork: name the child, or let the sergeant blame the stranger.
Maren: Well? You were out by the bridge last night. Who moves my stones? #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0100_Maren
-> It was Lio, the miller's child. #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0200
    <<set $culprit to Culprit.Lio>>
    Maren: The miller's own. That will please the steward. #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0300_Maren
    Maren: I'll have a word with Bram. A quiet word. The child gets a fright, and the stones stay put. #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0400_Maren
-> I saw nobody. #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0500
    <<set $culprit to Culprit.Pell>>
    <<set $pell_trust to $pell_trust - 2>>
    Maren: Nobody. Then it's the peddler. He came the same week as the stones started walking. #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0600_Maren
    Maren: Strangers always. #mood:angry #line:Maren.4aed2f04_0700_Maren
<<set $quest_stones to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed stones>>
===

title: Maren
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: $act != Act.Survey or $quest_stones == QuestState.Succeeded or $quest_stones == QuestState.Failed
---
=> Maren: The inn is the place to hear things. Hedda hears everything. #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0100_Maren
=> Maren: The castle wants a straight road. The mill wants to keep standing. I want a quiet fair. #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0200_Maren
=> Maren: Your map had better be right. People will fight over it. <<if survey_count() > 0>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0300_Maren
=> Maren: The Lockup is empty. Let us keep it that way. <<if $culprit != Culprit.Pell>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0400_Maren
=> Maren: The peddler sat in the Lockup a night, and the stones moved anyway. I don't like being wrong. <<if $culprit == Culprit.Pell and $act != Act.Survey>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0500_Maren
=> Maren: Back from the castle already? <<if $act == Act.Castle>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0600_Maren
=> Maren: Jory's mother hasn't slept. <<if $act == Act.Fair and not $jory_found>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0700_Maren
=> Maren: The fair has a hearing this year. I have twice the watch and half the patience. <<if $act == Act.Fair>> #line:Maren.0167d0b8_0800_Maren
===

title: Corvin
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: not $met_corvin
---
Corvin: You must be the cartographer. Corvin Hale, steward to the Countess. #line:Corvin.d3f61feb_0100_Corvin
Corvin: The new road will come down from the castle, straight across the bridge, past the mill and on to the market towns. #line:Corvin.d3f61feb_0200_Corvin
Corvin: Draw it so, and the castle will remember you kindly. #line:Corvin.d3f61feb_0300_Corvin
<<set $met_corvin to true>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $met_corvin
---
<<if $road == Road.Corvin>>
    Corvin: A straight road and a sensible map. We understand each other. #line:Corvin.a8c2e55b_0100_Corvin
<<elseif $road == Road.Miller>>
    Corvin: The miller's friend. I hope his flour pays better than the castle. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.a8c2e55b_0200_Corvin
<<elseif $road == Road.NoSide>>
    Corvin: Still drawing nothing at all? A map is a decision, cartographer. #line:Corvin.a8c2e55b_0300_Corvin
<<else>>
    Corvin: Have you spoken to the miller yet? He will tell you a sad story about a wheel. #line:Corvin.a8c2e55b_0400_Corvin
<<endif>>
===

title: Bram
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: not $met_bram
---
Bram: Bram Oster. The mill is mine, and my father's, and his father's. #line:Bram.e3b5468f_0100_Bram
Bram: Now the steward wants his road straight through my yard, and the mill down, so his carts don't have to turn a corner. #line:Bram.e3b5468f_0200_Bram
Bram: And on top of it the wheel is stuck. A cracked gear. If the mill can't grind, it might as well come down. #line:Bram.e3b5468f_0300_Bram
<<set $met_bram to true>>
<<set $quest_wheel to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed wheel>>
===

title: Bram
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
quest: wheel
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $met_bram and $quest_wheel == QuestState.Offered
---
Bram: A gear, that is all the wheel wants. The peddler might have one in his cart, if you can make him part with it. #line:Bram.dcabc1c3_0100_Bram
-> I will find you a gear. #line:Bram.dcabc1c3_0200
    Bram: Then you are a better friend than the steward. #line:Bram.dcabc1c3_0300_Bram
    <<set $quest_wheel to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed wheel>>
-> Not now. #line:Bram.dcabc1c3_0400
    Bram: Nobody ever has time for a wheel. #line:Bram.dcabc1c3_0500_Bram
===

title: Bram
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: not $bram_has_errand
---
=> Bram: Lio is in the mill. Shy, but sharp. Sharper than me with numbers. #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0100_Bram
=> Bram: My grandmother said the old border ran under the hill. Nobody listens to grandmothers. #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0200_Bram
=> Bram: The wheel turns. Listen to it! <<if $wheel_mended>> #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0300_Bram
=> Bram: Lio has been quiet since the sergeant came round. <<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>> #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0400_Bram
=> Bram: Fair day. The whole valley will hear where the road goes. <<if $act == Act.Fair>> #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0500_Bram
=> Bram: Thank you for speaking up. Whatever comes of it. <<if $spoke_for_mill>> #line:Bram.d5f8f1e5_0600_Bram
===

title: Stones
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: stones
when: $quest_stones == QuestState.Active and not $saw_lio
when: time_of_day() == "night"
---
// Only at night: the cartographer waits by the stones and sees who moves them.
You wait in the dark by the bridge. The river talks to itself. #line:Stones.80d1cc09_0100
A small figure comes down from the mill with a lantern under a coat. It is Lio, the miller's child. #line:Stones.80d1cc09_0200
Lio puts a shoulder to the nearest stone and rolls it two paces up the bank. #line:Stones.80d1cc09_0300
Lio: There. Where grandmother said. The old line runs under the hill, not along the river. #line:Stones.80d1cc09_0400_Lio
Lio sees you, and runs. #line:Stones.80d1cc09_0500
<<set $saw_lio to true>>
===

title: Stones
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: survey
when: not surveyed("stones")
---
Five grey boundary stones in a row along the bank, each with a mason's mark. One of them has fresh earth around it. #line:Stones.ad692b09_0100
<<survey stones>>
<<detour SurveyCheck>>
===

title: Stones
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
when: always
---
=> The boundary stones lean towards the river. One of them has moved again. #line:Stones.d9fd53f9_0100
=> Each stone carries the same mason's mark: a circle with a line through it. #line:Stones.d9fd53f9_0200
===

title: BridgeMark
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The commission
quest: survey
---
<<if surveyed("bridge")>>
    The bridge's height mark is already on your map. #line:BridgeMark_0100
<<else>>
    A mason cut a line in the bridge to mark the flood of the bad year. You take its height and its place. #line:BridgeMark_0200
    <<survey bridge>>
    <<detour SurveyCheck>>
<<endif>>
===

title: SurveyCheck
act: All
location: Anywhere
quest: survey
---
// Said after each landmark is put on the map.
<<if $quest_survey == QuestState.Active and surveyed("bell") and surveyed("well") and surveyed("loft") and surveyed("bridge") and surveyed("stones")>>
    The fifth landmark. The village is on your map, every stone of it. #line:SurveyCheck_0100
    <<set $quest_survey to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed survey>>
<<elseif $quest_survey == QuestState.Active>>
    [plural value={survey_count()} one="One landmark" other="% landmarks" /] out of five on the map. #line:SurveyCheck_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: Wheel
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
quest: wheel
when: $quest_wheel == QuestState.Active and has_item("gear")
---
You fit Pell's gear to the shaft, and lean on the spokes. The wheel groans, and turns, and the river takes it. #line:Wheel.fb9ae057_0100
Bram: It turns! Listen to it! #line:Wheel.fb9ae057_0200_Bram
Bram: Here, take my old rope. It held the sacks for twenty years. It will hold you anywhere you need to climb. #line:Wheel.fb9ae057_0300_Bram
<<take gear>>
<<give rope>>
<<set $wheel_mended to true>>
<<set $quest_wheel to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed wheel>>
===

title: Wheel
act: All
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: always
---
<<if $wheel_mended>>
    The wheel turns, and the mill hums behind it. #line:Wheel.f2c9d071_0100
<<else>>
    The wheel is stuck. One of the gears on the shaft is cracked through. #line:Wheel.f2c9d071_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: Nettle
act: All
location: Village
quest: herbs
when: not $nettle_taken
---
<<if $quest_herbs == QuestState.Active>>
    You pick the nettle with your sleeve over your hand. #line:Nettle.2748e52e_0100
    <<give nettle>>
    <<set $nettle_taken to true>>
<<else>>
    Nettles. Somebody might want them, but not you. #line:Nettle.2748e52e_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: DewCup
act: All
location: Village
quest: herbs
when: not $dewcup_taken
---
<<if $quest_herbs != QuestState.Active>>
    A dew-cup by the river, its blue cup full of water. #line:DewCup.93f0c1fe_0100
<<elseif time_of_day() != "morning">>
    The dew-cup has closed. They only open in the morning. #line:DewCup.93f0c1fe_0200
<<else>>
    You pick the dew-cup while it is still open and wet. #line:DewCup.93f0c1fe_0300
    <<give dewcup>>
    <<set $dewcup_taken to true>>
<<endif>>
===
